# Antigravity GUI Installation & Setup Guide (English)

[한국어 가이드](./antigravity.ko.md) · [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/releases/latest)

This guide walks you through installing and connecting the Claire Bible plugin using only the **Antigravity GUI** — no terminal commands or manual JSON editing required.

---

## Before You Start (1 Minute)

1. Sign in to your **Claire Bible** web interface.
2. Open **Account Settings** (`/settings/account`) and switch **Extraction mode** to **`Agent Client (client)`**.
3. Open **MCP Settings** (`/settings/mcp`) in your browser so your `/mcp` endpoint URL and quick setup prompt are ready to copy.

---

## Method 1 (Recommended): Paste Once in Antigravity Chat

You do not need to know where hidden plugin folders live or edit any configuration files.

1. On your Claire Bible **`/settings/mcp`** page, locate **Official Agent Marketplace (GitHub)** and click **Copy** next to **Antigravity quick setup prompt**.
   - If you are starting from GitHub directly, copy the prompt below and replace `https://<your-claire-server>/mcp` with your server's `/mcp` URL from `/settings/mcp`:
   ```text
   Install the claire-antigravity plugin (.zip) from the latest GitHub Release of https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}} into my Antigravity plugins folder, verify SHA256SUMS, and set the claire MCP server URL to https://<your-claire-server>/mcp.
   ```
2. Open the **Antigravity** app, start a **New Conversation**, paste the prompt, and send it.
3. Once Antigravity finishes installing the bundle, open **Customizations -> Installed -> MCP Servers** in the left sidebar.
4. Click **Authenticate** next to `claire`, sign in to your Claire Bible server in the browser, and approve the `readonly` and `write` scopes.

---

## Method 2 (Point-and-Click): Manual GUI Installation

Use this method if you prefer downloading the plugin yourself or if your environment restricts agent downloads. **No JSON file editing is needed.**

### Step 1: Download the `.zip` Bundle
1. Open the [GitHub Releases page](https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/releases/latest).
2. Under **Assets**, click **`claire-antigravity-v{{VERSION}}.zip`** to download it. (You do not need the `.tar.gz` file.)
3. Double-click the downloaded `.zip` file to extract the **`claire-antigravity`** folder. Check that `plugin.json` sits directly inside `claire-antigravity/`.

### Step 2: Move the Folder Into Antigravity Plugins
Open the plugins folder for your OS and move the extracted **`claire-antigravity`** folder inside. (If `plugins` does not exist yet inside `.gemini/config`, create an empty `plugins` folder first.)

- **macOS (Finder)**
  1. In Finder, choose **Go -> Go to Folder...** (`Command + Shift + G`).
  2. Enter `~/.gemini/config/plugins` and press **Return**.
  3. Drag the `claire-antigravity` folder into that window.
- **Windows (File Explorer)**
  1. Click the address bar at the top of File Explorer.
  2. Paste `%USERPROFILE%\.gemini\config\plugins` and press **Enter**.
  3. Move the `claire-antigravity` folder into that folder.
- **Linux (File Manager)**
  1. Open your Home folder and press `Ctrl + H` to show hidden folders.
  2. Open `.gemini` -> `config` -> `plugins` and move the `claire-antigravity` folder inside.

### Step 3: Add the MCP Server in Antigravity GUI
1. In the **Antigravity** app, open **Customizations -> Installed** in the left sidebar.
2. Confirm **`Claire Bible`** appears and is enabled.
3. Scroll to **MCP Servers** and click **Add MCP Server (+)**.
4. Enter:
   - **Name**: `claire`
   - **URL**: Your Claire Bible `/mcp` URL copied from `/settings/mcp` (for example, `https://claire.example.com/mcp`)
5. Save, then click **Authenticate** next to `claire` to approve OAuth 2.1 (`readonly` and `write`).

> **Avoid duplicate servers**: If you already ran Method 1, the `claire` MCP server is already configured. Choose either Method 1 or Method 2 — do not add a second `claire` entry.

---

## Verify Connection & Run Your First Extraction

Click any of the starter prompt chips on the **Claire Bible** plugin card in Antigravity, or paste one into a new chat:

- `List pending Claire Bible sources`
- `Extract and save pending Claire Bible sources`
- `Search topics in my Claire Bible knowledge graph`

Antigravity automatically delegates source reading and extraction to the isolated `claire-extractor` subagent (Claire MCP tools only, zero shell/file tools) and commits validated results into your personal knowledge base.

---

## FAQ & Troubleshooting

- **I cannot find the `.gemini` folder.**
  - Folders starting with `.` are hidden by default. Use `Command + Shift + G` on macOS Finder, paste `%USERPROFILE%\.gemini\config\plugins` into the Windows File Explorer address bar, or press `Ctrl + H` in Linux file managers.
- **`Claire Bible` does not appear under Customizations -> Installed.**
  - Make sure you did not create an extra nested folder (`plugins/claire-antigravity/claire-antigravity/plugin.json`). The file `plugin.json` must be directly at `plugins/claire-antigravity/plugin.json`.
- **Do I need to edit `mcp_config.json.tmpl` inside the folder?**
  - **No.** Leave `mcp_config.json.tmpl` untouched when configuring the server via **Add MCP Server (+)** in the GUI.
- **How do I update to a newer version?**
  - Run Method 1 again, or download the new `.zip` and replace the `plugins/claire-antigravity` folder. Your MCP server URL and OAuth login remain intact.

